Among black females, median (composite) wealth was $175 in 1985, $2,600 in 1990 and $4,000 in 1996 (nominal dollars). The largest increase occurred between 1985 and 1990, with an absolute rise of $2,425 (+1385.7%), exceeding the change between 1990 and 1996 (Δ$1,400). The full-period 1985->1996 rise (Δ$3,825) is the largest cumulative change.